For the full nonlinear system (2.2), linearisation around a desired synchronised operating point yields

\frac{d}{dt}\delta\mathbf{X}(t) = (\mathbf{I} \otimes \mathbf{A}_0) \delta\mathbf{X}(t) - (\mathbf{L}_\tau \otimes \mathbf{M}) \delta\mathbf{X}_t,

where \mathbf{L}_\tau is the delay‑structured supra‑Laplacian, \mathbf{M} encodes the coupling mechanism, and \delta\mathbf{X}_t is the history segment. The MSF extends to this case: stability is governed by the condition

