4.2 The Constitutional Fiber Bundle

Definition 4.2.1 (Base Space).
Let \mathcal{B} = (V, E, \tau) be the undirected physical settlement graph as before, with vertices V = \{1,\dots,N\} and edges weighted by light‑time delays \tau_{ij}.

Definition 4.2.2 (Constitutional Fiber).
For each settlement i, the constitutional fiber \mathcal{C}_i is a smooth Riemannian manifold of admissible local constitutions. A point \Theta_i \in \mathcal{C}_i is a tuple of legal parameters; the metric g_i measures “legal distance.”

Definition 4.2.3 (Constitutional Fiber Bundle).
The constitutional fiber bundle \mathcal{E} is the disjoint union \bigsqcup_{i \in V} \mathcal{C}_i with projection \pi: \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{B}, \pi(\Theta_i) = i. A global constitution is a section \sigma: \mathcal{B} \to \mathcal{E} satisfying \pi \circ \sigma = \text{id}_{\mathcal{B}}. The civilisational state at time t is a time‑dependent section \sigma_t.

