B.5 Proof of Theorem 3.5.1 (Consensus Decoupling via Laplacian)

Statement. The multi-agent system \dot{\mathbf{x}} = \sum (\mathbf{I} \otimes \mathbf{A}_d) \mathbf{x}(t-\tau_d) + \sum (\mathbf{L} \otimes \mathbf{B}\mathbf{K}_d\mathbf{C}) \mathbf{x}(t-\tau_d - \tau_c) decouples under \tilde{\mathbf{x}} = (\mathbf{U}^T \otimes \mathbf{I}) \mathbf{x} into N-1 independent subsystems, each with effective Laplacian eigenvalue \lambda_i.

Proof. Since \mathbf{U}^T \mathbf{L} \mathbf{U} = \boldsymbol{\Lambda}, we have \mathbf{L} = \mathbf{U} \boldsymbol{\Lambda} \mathbf{U}^T. Substituting and using the mixed-product property of Kronecker products, (\mathbf{L} \otimes \mathbf{M}) = (\mathbf{U} \otimes \mathbf{I})(\boldsymbol{\Lambda} \otimes \mathbf{M})(\mathbf{U}^T \otimes \mathbf{I}). Apply this to the dynamics. The transformed state \tilde{\mathbf{x}}_i (rows of \tilde{\mathbf{x}}) satisfy

\dot{\tilde{\mathbf{x}}}_i = \sum_d \mathbf{A}_d \tilde{\mathbf{x}}_i(t-\tau_d) + \lambda_i \sum_d \mathbf{B}\mathbf{K}_d\mathbf{C} \tilde{\mathbf{x}}_i(t-\tau_d - \tau_c),

for i=2,\dots,N. The first component (i=1) corresponds to the consensus mode and is unaffected. ∎

