B.6 Proof of Theorem 3.6.1 (Control-Rate Governability Bound)

Statement. If the open-loop constitutional divergence has topological entropy h(\mathbf{A}), then any stabilising controller requires channel capacity C \ge h(\mathbf{A})/\ln 2.

Proof. This is a direct application of the data-rate theorem (Nair & Evans, 2004). The unstable part of the linearised system generates uncertainty at rate h(\mathbf{A}). By the theorem, the feedback channel must supply information at least at this rate to ensure bounded state estimation error. The bound is independent of delay as long as the channel provides anytime reliability. ∎

