B.7 Proof of Theorem 4.3.2 (Functoriality of Civilisation Evolution)

Statement. The time-evolution operator \mathcal{E}_t on the category \mathbf{Civ} is an endofunctor: \mathcal{E}_{t_1 + t_2} = \mathcal{E}_{t_1} \circ \mathcal{E}_{t_2} and \mathcal{E}_0 = \text{id}.

Proof. The civilisation state is the solution of a DDE with Lipschitz dynamics. By uniqueness (Theorem 2.2.1), evolution from time 0 to t_1+t_2 is the same as evolution to t_1 followed by evolution for t_2. The identity at t=0 is trivial. On morphisms (civilisation transformations), we define \mathcal{E}_t(f) as the transformation induced by advancing the state by t; this respects composition because the dynamics are autonomous and deterministic. ∎

