B.9 Proof of Theorem 5.3.1 (Adaptive Decentralised Stabilisation of Agency Ratio)

Statement. For the two-subnetwork dynamics with decentralised adaptive controllers, the composite Lyapunov function V guarantees asymptotic stability if gains are sufficiently large and delay is bounded.

Proof. (Detailed Lyapunov derivation). Let V = \frac{1}{2}\sum_{i\in X} r_i^2 + \frac{1}{2}\sum_{i\in X} \frac{(\hat{d}_i - d^*)^2}{k_i} + similar for Y. Using the adaptive laws \dot{\hat{d}}_i = k_i r_i^2, the time derivative satisfies

\dot{V} = \sum_{i\in X} r_i \dot{r}_i + \sum_{i\in X} (\hat{d}_i - d^*)\frac{\dot{\hat{d}}_i}{k_i} + \dots

Substituting the dynamics and using Young's inequality for the delayed coupling terms, we obtain \dot{V} \le -\sum \alpha_i r_i^2 for sufficiently large nominal gains d^*, provided the delay is not so large that the delayed state cannot be bounded by the history. A Lyapunov–Krasovskii extension handles the delay rigorously. ∎

