r = \lambda r \int_{-\pi/2}^{\pi/2} \cos^2\theta \, g(\omega_0 - \lambda r \sin\theta) d\theta,

with a modification due to the delay: the effective coupling becomes \lambda \cos(\omega_0 \tau) where \omega_0 is the mean frequency. The onset of a non-zero solution occurs when \lambda \cos(\omega_0 \tau) = 2/(\pi g(0)). The largest eigenvalue \lambda_{\max}(\tau) of the delay-attenuated adjacency matrix replaces \cos(\omega_0 \tau) in the network case. ∎

