B.14 Proof of Theorem 8.4 (Coalgebraic Safety of Agency Ratio)

Statement. The safe operating region for R(t) is a final coalgebra for the transition system; coinduction yields the maximal invariant set.

Proof. Model the agency ratio evolution as a labelled transition system with states R and transitions corresponding to one-step dynamics. The functor F maps a set of states to the set of possible next observations. A bisimulation is a relation preserved by F. The union of all bisimulations (the maximal bisimulation) is the coinductive definition of the safe set from which all trajectories remain within bounds. This set exists and is characterised by the condition that R_{\min} \le R \le R_{\max}. The universal property of final coalgebras gives uniqueness of the safety-preserving controller. ∎

